{
  "statement": "Ethical and compliance considerations are critical for the ATM system. Ensuring transactions comply with financial regulations (RES-01) protects both the bank and its clients. Comprehensive transaction logs (RES-02) support accountability and transparency. Preventing negative account balances (RES-03) aligns with fair banking practices, while validating user identity through secure PIN (RES-04) safeguards client information. Automatically withdrawing funds only when sufficient (RES-05) ensures responsible banking, and immediate notifications of insufficient funds (RES-06) enhance user awareness. Lastly, maintaining user privacy (RES-07) is essential for client trust and compliance with data protection laws.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-01", "TRU-04"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "Both SAF-01 and TRU-04 prevent negative balances, but they are framed in different contexts, leading to potential conflict in enforcement."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-06", "RES-06"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "EFF-06 emphasizes immediate feedback on withdrawal requests, while RES-06 focuses on notifying users of insufficient funds; these may overlap and cause confusion."
    }
  ],
